powerpagecomponent.content:
{
  "description": "Exposes contact to the portal Web API so a checker can request a claim. Paired with a one-column allowlist: the only writable column is al_claimrequest, which ClaimRequestPlugin reads. The browser used to POST an al_caseassignment carrying two @odata.bind lookups instead; Power Pages refused that association with 90040106 through three verified permission repairs, the same refusal and the same resolution as the answering module (AD-053). Writing a contact rather than an assignment is also the stronger boundary: the contact permission is Self-scoped, so the request can only reach the signed-in user's own row, and the plug-in takes the claimant from that row rather than from the payload.",
  "value": "true"
}
